  "notes": "{冷却|れいきゃく} combines {冷|れい} (cold) + {却|きゃく} (withdraw), referring to the process of reducing temperature. Primarily a technical/scientific term.\n\nUSAGE:\nMost common in technical and industrial contexts. Also used figuratively: {冷却|れいきゃく}{期間|きかん} means a \"cooling-off period\" for emotions or negotiations.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {冷却|れいきゃく}する: to cool\n- {冷却|れいきゃく}{装置|そうち}: cooling system/device\n- {冷却|れいきゃく}{水|すい}: coolant water\n- {冷却|れいきゃく}{期間|きかん}: cooling-off period\n- {冷却|れいきゃく}ファン: cooling fan\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {冷|ひ}やす: to cool (everyday, e.g. food/drinks)\n- {冷凍|れいとう}: freezing (below 0°C)\n- {冷蔵|れいぞう}: refrigeration (above 0°C)\n- {加熱|かねつ}: heating (opposite process)",
